---
import StarLayout from "@/layouts/StarLayout.astro";
---

<StarLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="How mauroner.net handles analytics, browser-local tools, provider connections, and contact requests."
>
  <article class="prose prose-slate mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12 dark:prose-invert sm:px-6">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p><strong>Effective date:</strong> 14 July 2026</p>

    <h2>Who operates this site</h2>
    <p>
      Maximilian Mauroner operates mauroner.net. Privacy questions and deletion
      requests can be sent to <a href="mailto:home@relay.mauroner.net">home@relay.mauroner.net</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Public-page analytics</h2>
    <p>
      Analytics is off unless you explicitly enable it below. When enabled, public
      pages send page-view events to an EU-hosted PostHog project. Automatic click
      capture and session recording are disabled, and the browser identity is held
      in memory instead of a persistent analytics cookie or local-storage ID.
      PostHog and its infrastructure can still process request metadata such as the
      page URL, referrer, IP address, browser, and device information. Event
      retention is controlled by the PostHog project; contact the address above to
      ask for access or deletion.
    </p>
    <p>
      Analytics is never loaded on admin pages or the Leaveify, Readwise Tags
      Mapper, Spotify History, and WhatsApp Stats tools, regardless of this choice.
    </p>

    <div class="not-prose my-6 rounded-lg border border-border bg-muted/50 p-4">
      <p id="analytics-status" class="mb-3 text-sm" role="status" aria-live="polite">
        Checking your analytics preference…
      </p>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        <button type="button" class="site-action" data-analytics-choice="granted">
          Enable public-page analytics
        </button>
        <button type="button" class="site-action" data-analytics-choice="denied">
          Disable analytics
        </button>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2>Tools and uploaded files</h2>
    <p>
      WhatsApp Stats and Spotify History parse selected exports in your browser;
      the site does not upload those archives for analysis. Readwise Tags Mapper
      sends requests needed to communicate with Readwise. Leaveify sends the
      selected library data to the music providers involved in the transfer. Those
      providers apply their own privacy terms. Browser-local storage may retain
      tool state until you clear it.
    </p>

    <h2>Hosting and ordinary server logs</h2>
    <p>
      The hosting and network providers necessarily process requests to deliver the
      site and may keep operational or security logs. Do not send secrets through
      the public contact or content pages.
    </p>
  </article>

  <script>
    const status = document.getElementById("analytics-status");
    const updateStatus = () => {
      if (!status) return;
      const choice = localStorage.getItem("analytics-consent");
      status.textContent =
        choice === "granted"
          ? "Public-page analytics is enabled."
          : "Public-page analytics is disabled.";
    };

    document.addEventListener("click", (event) => {
      if (!(event.target instanceof Element)) return;
      const button = event.target.closest("[data-analytics-choice]");
      if (!(button instanceof HTMLButtonElement)) return;
      const choice = button.dataset.analyticsChoice;
      if (choice !== "granted" && choice !== "denied") return;
      localStorage.setItem("analytics-consent", choice);
      updateStatus();
      if (choice === "granted") window.location.reload();
      else {
        const analyticsWindow = window as Window & {
          posthog?: { opt_out_capturing?: () => void };
        };
        analyticsWindow.posthog?.opt_out_capturing?.();
      }
    });

    updateStatus();
    document.addEventListener("astro:after-swap", updateStatus);
  </script>
</StarLayout>
